# WebMCP Origin Trial token.
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` and paste your own token. `.env.local` is gitignored; a token is
# bound to one origin, so ours would not work for you anyway.
#
# Register at https://developer.chrome.com/origintrials — pick the WebMCP / Prompt API trial, and
# request one token per origin you serve from (http://localhost:3000 and your deployed URL are two
# different origins).
#
# Leave it empty and Veil still runs: `src/lib/webmcp/polyfill.ts` installs a stand-in
# `document.modelContext` so the tools can be exercised from the debug panel without a browser that
# implements the API. What you lose is the only thing that matters for the demo — a real agent
# calling the tools.
NEXT_PUBLIC_WEBMCP_ORIGIN_TRIAL_TOKEN=

# Origins allowed to see the reveal tools.
#
# Comma-separated, no spaces. Tools that can uncover a value are registered with
# `exposedTo: [...]` so that only agents you name can even see they exist; every other origin gets
# the read-only analysis set. See `docs/tools.md` § Origin layering.
#
# Empty means "expose the reveal tools to everyone", which is the right default for local
# development and the wrong one for a deployment you have shared a link to.
NEXT_PUBLIC_VEIL_TRUSTED_ORIGINS=
